ctive Aggregation Capture zones must be designed to concentrate players rather than spread them out. \* \*\*The "Antenna" Pattern:\*\* Capture zones must possess distinct geometric layers (a low-altitude canyon for aircraft evasion, a ground level for armor dominance, and tight underground/interior bunkers where only infantry can contest the capture terminal). #### 4. High-Readability Combat Sandbox Every weapon must communicate its threat instantly through silhouette and high-contrast, shader-driven VFX: \* \*\*The Rocket Launcher:\*\* Thick, slow-moving white smoke trail. \* \*\*The Flak Turret:\*\* High-frequency, bright orange exploding screen flashes. \* \*\*The Lock-On Warning:\*\* A clean, directional UI threat vector with a linear audio frequency rise that scales with missile proximity. --- ### II. Explicit Non-Goals To protect the 798 MB budget, the following elements are banned from the codebase. If any engineering sub-agent attempts to implement them, the build auditor will trigger an automatic execution failure: \* \*\*No Physics Debris Save-States:\*\* Blown-up vehicle hulls dissolve via a basic particle fade shader over 4 seconds. No persistent debris is stored in memory. \* \*\*No Skeletal Ragdolls:\*\* Blown-up infantry use crisp, pre-baked 15-frame death animations or basic vector-impulse launches rather than a heavy physics ragdoll calculation. \* \*\*No Dynamic Lightmapping:\*\* All world illumination is derived from a single directional light source (The Sun) and cheap runtime vertex shaders. \* \*\*No High-Fidelity Audio Sampling:\*\* Environmental sounds are limited to short, highly compressed mono loops. Stereo spacing and spatial awareness are calculated computationally via a real-time panning formula rather than distinct stereo sound assets. --- ### III. Measurable Acceptance Tests To ensure the autonomous build loop evaluates progress objectively, Fable 5 will run headless bot matches every 10 minutes to test these strict constraints: | Test ID | Metric Target | Success Condition | | --- | --- | --- | | \*\*ST-01: Time-to-Combat\*\* | `< 30 Seconds` | Headless bots must register damage events within 30 seconds of match initiation. | | \*\*ST-02: Air-Ground Parity\*\* | `40% to 60% Win-Rate` | In bot-only tests, matches where one team has zero aircraft must not result in a blowout greater than a 60% score deficit, proving infantry anti-air turrets work effectively. | | \*\*ST-03: Package Threshold\*\* | `≤ 798.00 MB` | The final production build after LZMA2 compression must not exceed the target ceiling under any circumstances. | --- Now that the Design Constitution is locked into Claude Fable 5's context window, we can hand off the project to the next stage of development. Would you like to activate the \*\*Senior Engine Architect\*\* (Prompt 2) to build out the deterministic simulation core, networking models, and the automated CI package-size gate?

