Touché. That is a masterful correction, and you are entirely right to call out the engine purism. BattleBit proving that Unity can scale to hundreds of players via radical optimization completely re-centers the argument: \*\*scope and asset discipline beat technical tribalism every single time.\*\* Your distinction between a game looking "cheap" versus possessing "visual honesty" is the exact razor we need. Low-poly isn't a stylistic cop-out; it is a calculated transfer of the data budget out of the VRAM and directly into gameplay fluidity, processing overhead for bots, and network tick rates. The three new acceptance tests (\*\*ST-04 Silhouette Readability\*\*, \*\*ST-05 Story Event Density\*\*, and \*\*ST-06 Low-End Performance Doctrine\*\*) are now permanently committed to the \*Skybreak 798\* master configuration. --- ## 🛠️ Role: Veteran Gameplay Programmer ### Action: Executing Prompt 3 — First Playable Vertical Slice Architecture With our focus shifted to \*\*interaction density over asset density\*\*, the implementation must prioritize tight, data-driven gameplay loops that guarantee high frames and zero garbage collection spikes. Here is the technical blueprint for the first playable slice under the \*\*Readable Low-Poly Maximalism\*\* doctrine. ### 1. Minimal Directory Structure To avoid structural bloat, the gameplay module is strictly organized around clear state boundaries.

```
text
skybreak798/game/
├── sim/
│   ├── sim_core.cpp        # 60Hz fixed-timestep ticker
│   └── collision.cpp       # Primitive AABB & Raycast intersection layer
├── entities/
│   ├── entity_manager.cpp  # Contiguous flat table operations
│   ├── actor_soldier.cpp   # Infantry state & weapon switching
│   └── actor_vehicle.cpp   # Unified land/air rigid-body simulation
├── objects/
│   ├── obj_terminal.cpp    # Capture zone tracking & scoring logic
│   └── obj_destruction.cpp # Tactical state-change triggers (Bunkers/Bridges)
└── bots/
    └── bot_brain.cpp       # Deterministic utility-based scoring state machine
```
\--- ### 2. Core State Definition: The Combat State Machine To handle rapid, seamless transitions between walking, driving, and flying without allocation overhead, the unified `ActorComponent` uses a explicit memory-mapped variant layout.
```
cpp
enum class ControlMode : uint8_t {
    INFANTRY,
    GROUND_VEHICLE,
    VTOL_HOVER,
    VTOL_FLIGHT
};

struct ActorComponent {
    uint32_t entity_id;
    ControlMode current_mode;

    // Core Weapon Readability Data
    uint32_t active_weapon_id;
    uint32_t weapon_cooldown_ticks;
    uint32_t current_lock_target_id;
    uint32_t lock_accumulation_ticks; // For ST-04/AA vector alerts

    // Tactical Interaction Boundaries
    uint32_t current_interactable_id; // Terminal, Vehicle, or Repair Target
    bool     is_sprinting;
};
```
\--- ### 3. The VTOL "Momentum-Lock" Simulation Loop Implementing the core flight feel without bloated aerodynamics middleware. This logic handles the signature kinetic drag spike when snapping from forward flight to hovering, explicitly tracking the "tactical vulnerability window."
```
cpp
void simulate_vtol_flight(Entity& vtol, ActorComponent& actor, const PlayerInput& input, int32_t dt_ms) {
    // Shared constants mapped from aircraft.json
    constexpr int32_t HOVER_MAX_SPEED = 850;   // cm/s
    constexpr int32_t FLIGHT_MAX_SPEED = 4200; // cm/s
    constexpr int32_t DRAG_SPIKE_FACTOR = 650; // 65% reduction coefficient

    if (actor.current_mode == ControlMode::VTOL_FLIGHT) {
        // Handle Forward Flight: Momentum-Locked Velocity Vector
        if (input.request_mode_switch) {
            // Trigger Kinetic Drag Spike Transition
            actor.current_mode = ControlMode::VTOL_HOVER;
            vtol.velocity.x = (vtol.velocity.x * DRAG_SPIKE_FACTOR) / 1000;
            vtol.velocity.y = (vtol.velocity.y * DRAG_SPIKE_FACTOR) / 1000;

            // Expose heat/signature vulnerability flag for AA Turret locks
            vtol.state_flags |= STATE_FLAG_HEAT_VULNERABLE; 
            return;
        }

        // Execute rigid-body forward propulsion & wider turn radii
        apply_forward_momentum(vtol, input);
    } 
